# MainstreetAi — AI role keys
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and paste your keys. Both roles are inert without
# one: the simulation falls back to its validated rules-based policy and the
# three built-in scenarios, so nothing breaks if you leave these blank.
#
# Two keys, not one, on purpose. The emulator invents traffic; the orchestrator
# influences signal timing. Separate credentials mean you can budget,
# rate-limit, revoke and audit them independently, and a compromised scenario
# generator has no path to the control loop.
#
# The provider is inferred from the key's prefix, so pasting a key is usually
# all you need:
#     AIza… / AQ.…   -> gemini
#     nvapi-…        -> nvidia
#     sk-ant-…       -> anthropic

# Scenario emulation: a description in, structured traffic events out.
MAINSTREET_EMULATOR_KEY=

# Signal orchestration: reads live network state, returns signal policy.
MAINSTREET_ORCHESTRATOR_KEY=

# --- optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# Override the inferred provider if ever needed: gemini | nvidia | anthropic
# MAINSTREET_EMULATOR_PROVIDER=gemini
# MAINSTREET_ORCHESTRATOR_PROVIDER=nvidia

# Pin a model. Leaving these unset uses the provider's fallback chain, which is
# the safer choice — see below.
# MAINSTREET_EMULATOR_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# MAINSTREET_ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL=mistralai/mistral-nemotron

# Ordered fallback models, tried until one answers. Defaults per provider are in
# ai/config.py. This is not over-engineering: building this hit a retired model
# (404 "no longer available to new users"), a model at capacity (503), and
# models that accept the connection and never respond — all within an hour, all
# on live endpoints. None of those are things you control on the day.
# MAINSTREET_EMULATOR_FALLBACKS=gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3-flash-preview,gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# Keep the keys in place but run the deterministic baseline — useful when you
# want a reproducible A/B without deleting your configuration.
# MAINSTREET_ORCHESTRATOR_DISABLED=true
# MAINSTREET_EMULATOR_DISABLED=true
